ring. I therefore cannot verify that any hop lies within [18031,56431] or that successive hops are separated by <=600 time units, which is the defining requirement of the claim. The high degree/triangle counts of 45, 153 and 1680 show the static path is plausibly hub-mixing artefact rather than a specific influence chain, and a crude prior gives ~0.002 probability of an accidental delta<=600 chain - but neither confirms nor refutes the cascade. Verdict: insufficient temporal evidence.", "evidence": [{"trace_id": "step_01", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_13", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_06", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_07", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_08", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_03", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_04", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_14", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_20", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_22", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_02", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_09", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_10", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_11", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_21", "role": "confounder_control"}]}, "raw_final_response": "## Investigation Summary\n\n**What I could establish (static structure):**\n- The graph has 16,325 events over [0, 100000], 15,767 distinct edges, repeat ratio 0.034 \u2014 i.e. nearly every edge fires exactly once (step_01).\n- 1006 is a low-activity node (9 events, 9 partners); 1860 likewise (11 events) (step_02). Neither is a hub, so \"popularity\" is not an explanation.\n- There is **no direct edge** 1006 \u2192 1860 (step_13).\n- Static 3-hop routes do exist: 1006\u219245\u2192153\u21921860 (step_03, step_04, step_06, step_07, step_08), 1006\u21921680\u2192153\u21921860 (step_14, step_20), 1006\u2192475\u2192618\u21921860 (step_17, step_22). Each hop is carried by a **single** event (n_events = 1), so any cascade must use those exact events.\n- The intermediaries 45, 153, 1680 are high-degree brokers (126\u2013253 partners, 1433 triangles at 153; step_09, step_10, step_11), so the static connection is largely explained by hub-mediated mixing rather than a specific chain \u2014 a classic confounder for cascade claims.\n\n**What I could not establish (the decisive part):** every available tool reports whole-horizon aggregates only. No tool returns event timestamps, per-event ordering, or window-restricted counts, so I cannot check (a) whether any of these hop events fall inside [18031, 56431], nor (b) whether consecutive hops are ordered with gaps \u2264 600. A rough prior (single-shot edges, \u0394/horizon = 0.006, ~5 candidate 3-hop routes) puts the chance of an accidental \u0394\u2264600 chain at ~10\u207b\u00b3 (step_21), but that is a prior, not temporal evidence \u2014 and it cannot be used to *confirm* a cascade either.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_30df0d06\",\n  \"decision\": \"insufficient\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"cascade\",\n  \"entities\": [1006, 1860, 45, 153, 1680, 475, 618],\n  \"window\": [18031, 56431],\n  \"confidence\": 0.6,\n  \"narrative\": \"Static connectivity from 1006 to 1860 exists only via 3-hop routes through hub intermediaries (1006->45->153->1860, 1006->1680->153->1860, 1006->475->618->1860); there is no direct 1006->1860 edge. Each required hop is supported by exactly one event, and the observation tools expose only whole-horizon aggregates with no timestamps, no event ordering, and no window filtering. I therefore cannot verify that any hop lies within [18031,56431] or that successive hops are separated by <=600 time units, which is the defining requirement of the claim. The high degree/triangle counts of 45, 153 and 1680 show the static path is plausibly hub-mixing artefact rather than a specific influence chain, and a crude prior gives ~0.002 probability of an accidental delta<=600 chain - but neither confirms nor refutes the cascade. Verdict: insufficient temporal evidence.\",\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_01\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_13\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_06\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_07\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_08\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_03\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_04\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_14\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_20\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_22\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_02\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_09\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_10\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_11\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_21\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"}\n  ]\n}\n```", "total_input_tokens": 53785, "total_output_tokens": 8459, "total_tokens": 62244, "total_latency_ms": 125243, "llm_calls": 10, "schema_repairs": 0, "status": "success", "error": ""}